Function propagateLoadImagePanel()
  {
    return_type void
    open
  }
  {
    code {auto wn = cast(WidgetNode) currentWidgetNode_;
if (wn is null) return;

// The dimensions come from the image the live widget already loaded, so
// every format the canvas can show is readable here, and the path is
// resolved the same way.
auto liveW = liveTree_.widgetOf.get(wn, null);
if (wn.imageFilename.length)
  \{
    auto img = liveW is null ? null : liveW.image();
    if (img !is null)
      \{
        imagePanelData.label(format("%d x %d pixels, %d channels", img.dataW(), img.dataH(), img.d()));
      \}
    else
      \{
        imagePanelData.label("Can't load image");
      \}
    imagePanelImagegroup.activate();
  \}
else
  \{
    imagePanelData.label("... x ... pixels, ...");
    imagePanelImagegroup.deactivate();
  \}
imagePanelImageW.value(to!string(wn.scaleImageW));
imagePanelImageH.value(to!string(wn.scaleImageH));
imagePanelConvert.value(!wn.compressImage);
imagePanelBind.value(wn.bindImage);

if (wn.deimageFilename.length)
  \{
    auto dimg = liveW is null ? null : liveW.deimage();
    if (dimg !is null)
      \{
        imagePanelDedata.label(format("%d x %d pixels, %d channels", dimg.dataW(), dimg.dataH(), dimg.d()));
      \}
    else
      \{
        imagePanelDedata.label("Can't load image");
      \}
    imagePanelDeimagegroup.activate();
  \}
else
  \{
    imagePanelDedata.label("... x ... pixels, ...");
    imagePanelDeimagegroup.deactivate();
  \}
imagePanelDeimageW.value(to!string(wn.scaleDeimageW));
imagePanelDeimageH.value(to!string(wn.scaleDeimageH));
imagePanelDeconvert.value(!wn.compressDeimage);
imagePanelDebind.value(wn.bindDeimage);}
      {
      }
  }
Function runImagePanel()
  {
    return_type void
    open
  }
  {
    code {if (imagePanelWindow is null)
  \{
    makeImagePanel();
    wireEditHooks(imagePanelWindow);
  \}

propagateLoadImagePanel();

auto previousGrab = fl.core.grab();
if (previousGrab !is null) fl.core.grab(null);
imagePanelWindow.setModal();
imagePanelWindow.show();
while (imagePanelWindow.shown())
  fl.core.wait();
fl.core.grab(previousGrab);}
      {
      }
  }
comment {Every page of `tabs_wizard` is converted to this port's D
dialect (see TRANSLITERATION_GUIDE.md for the technique): code_tabs,
codeblock_tabs, class_tabs, declblock_tabs, decl_tabs, comment_tabs,
data_tabs, func_tabs (all 8 of tabs_wizard's non-widget-kind pages),
widgetTabsRepo (the permanently-hidden vestigial page), the bottom bar
(Live Resize/Hide Overlays/Close; `gui_main.d` supplies their
implementations, see the comment near the end of this file), and
widget_tabs itself (tabs_wizard's 9th and by far largest page, with its
GUI, Style and D sub-tabs). `thePanel`/`tabsWizard` (FLTK's own
anonymous `Fl_Window`/`tabs_wizard`) are placed too.

FLTK's own file-header boilerplate (C++-only `header_name`/
`code_name`/`include_guard`/`snap`/`mergeback` directives, ~20 raw
`decl \{\#include ...\}`/`extern`/`\#define` blocks, and the 4 dead
top-of-file C++ helpers -- `use_tab_navigation`/`update_current` x2/
`w_code_cb`) is dropped, along with the C++-only `flex_margin_cb`
helper (superseded by widget_tabs's own inline `onFlexMarginChanged()`).
The image-options dialog (`make_image_panel()`/`run_image_panel()`) is
`makeImagePanel()`/`propagateLoadImagePanel()`/`runImagePanel()` -- the
"..." button next to the Image field calls it. The scale-width/height
fields write `WidgetNode.scaleImageW`/etc; the edit hooks
(`wireEditHooks()`) then re-apply the node to its live widget
(`applyProperties()` re-scales the image and redraws the widget and its
parent). The dimension readout reads the natural size of the image the
live widget loaded.

The two embedded Grid sub-panels (`widgetTabGrid`/`widgetTabGridChild`,
`class GridTab`/`class GridChildTab`) live in their own files,
`panels/widget_panel_grid_tab.fl`/`widget_panel_grid_child_tab.fl`,
each a `widget_class` with its own public `load()` method -- imported
explicitly by the two `decl` lines near this file's own top, since
their file names don't match their class names (D resolves an import by
file name, so an automatic class-name-based guess would be wrong here;
see those two files' own top comments).
`propagateLoadWidget()` reparents them into/out of `widgetTabs` and
calls their `load()` based on whether the selection is a `GridNode` or
a `GridNode`'s own child, matching FLTK's reparenting logic.

`gui_main.d` imports this file's own generated entry points directly
(`make_widget_panel`/`load`/`current`/`refreshCodeFromNode`/
`wireEditHooks`/`onBeforeEdit`/`onEdited`/`onOpenExternalEditor`/
`overlayCb`/`okCb`/`thePanel`/`widgetTabs`). Multi-select apply: most
field callbacks loop over the whole selection, matching FLTK's
per-field behavior; a small set (widget name, Resizable, Hotspot,
Border/Modal/Nonmodal) stays single-target because FLTK's own callback
does too -- see the "---- widget_tabs ----" comment block further below
for the field-by-field writeup.

Live-canvas-widget updates and undo-checkpoint calls go through
`onBeforeEdit`/`onEdited`/`wireEditHooks()` -- see that same comment
block and the "gui_main.d integration surface" comment just above the
`onBeforeEdit`/`onEdited`/`onOpenExternalEditor` declarations.

Per-page state (currentCodeNode_ etc. below) and each page's own
propagateLoadX() function live here, next to make_widget_panel()
itself. FLTK reads `current_node`/`current_widget` globals (from
Fluid.h, not declared in this file); each converted page here tracks
which node it is showing explicitly, passed in as a parameter.

`fluid.comment_node.CommentNode` (FLTK's `Comment_Node`, a standalone
project-tree comment entry with `in_h_`/`in_c_` flags) backs
comment_tabs; it is wired into `fluid.factory`'s "comment" registry and
round-tripped through `project_writer.d`.
}
  {
    in_source
    in_header
  }
decl {import fluid;}
  {
    private
    local
