comment {`liveModeCb`/`overlayCb`/`okCb` (the bottom bar's own three
buttons) have empty bodies *in this file*, and are implemented in
`gui_main.d`. A Function referenced only as a bare `.callback(name)`
value (as all three are, from `wLiveMode`/`overlayButton`/the Close
`ReturnButton` respectively) is classified callback-shaped by
`code_writer.d` and becomes a module-level `void delegate(Widget) name;`
variable instead of an ordinary function -- and `code_writer.d`'s own
`generate()` only ever emits a callback-shaped Function's *body* as an
assignment inside a `main()`-shaped root Function
(`writeFunctionBody(mainFn, callbackFns)`, gated on `mainFn !is null`).
This file has no anonymous root Function (it is a panel, not a
program), so `mainFn` is always null here and any code written into one
of these three Functions' own `code` block would be generated nowhere:
the delegate variable would stay permanently null. The three stay
`void delegate(Widget)` variables (public, matching
`fluid.function_panel`'s own `binButtonCb`/`codeButtonCb`) that
`gui_main.d` assigns externally: `liveModeCb` runs Live Resize
(ported from FLTK's `live_mode_cb()`), `overlayCb` forwards to
`toggleOverlays()`, and `okCb` closes the panel.}
  {
    in_source
    in_header
  }
